"Goodness of fit compares one variable with a hypothesized distribution (df = categories − {#}, less one more for each parameter estimated from the data). Independence asks whether two variables of one sample are related; homogeneity asks whether several samples share one distribution. Both use E = (row total)(column total)/(grand total) and df = (rows − {#})(columns − {#}).",
